--- published post ---
# The Slumber of the Naiad

She rests where the current slows, a creature born of the river's slow breath and the damp earth, where the moss beneath her body is a soft, living velvet cradling her form as the day begins its long retreat. In the distance, the sun hangs low and heavy, a golden eye casting its warm, amber gaze across the winding waters while the reeds sway in silent homage to the fading day. To look upon her is to witness the quietude of a forgotten age, an eternal guardian of the quiet places waiting for the stars to claim the sky. Be Art. Be Unique.

> The river remembers every shadow that has ever crossed its waters, and so do I.

